Optional Adobe file-format plugins for Falcor2's private, core-only OpenUSD.

The core package contains shared utilities and does not require the FBX SDK.
No port features are enabled by default. Select usd-fileformat-plugins[fbx] to
build the FBX plugin. In Falcor2, FALCOR_ENABLE_USD_FBX=ON selects usd-fbx, which
explicitly requests that port feature.

The FBX feature downloads and verifies the platform's Autodesk FBX SDK 2020.3.11, then
extracts it into the port's build directory without running the installer.
No system-wide SDK installation is required. The SDK is linked statically;
Autodesk's SDK license applies and its notice is included in this package.
The overlay targets Windows x64, Linux x64, and macOS x64/arm64.

To use an existing copy of the same SDK, set FBXSDK_ROOT and add FBXSDK_ROOT to
VCPKG_KEEP_ENV_VARS before configuring. Both Debug and Release library hashes
must match the pinned platform SDK. Unset FBXSDK_ROOT to use automatic acquisition.

With the FBX feature enabled, Release registry:
  <triplet>/share/usd-fileformat-plugins/plugin/usdFbx/resources/plugInfo.json
Debug registry:
  <triplet>/debug/share/usd-fileformat-plugins/plugin/usdFbx/resources/plugInfo.json

On Windows, add <triplet>/bin to the DLL search path and preload
<triplet>/bin/falcor2_adobe_usdFbx.dll using ctypes.WinDLL(absolute_path), and call
falcor2.pxr.Plug.Registry().RegisterPlugins(<absolute registry filename>).
Keep the os.add_dll_directory() and DLL handles alive. Preloading supplies
Python's dependency search flags that USD's LoadLibrary call does not use.
Use debug/bin and the Debug registry only with the Debug Falcor2 runtime.

On Linux/macOS, register the same registry path; the plugin is installed under
<triplet>/lib as libfalcor2_adobe_usdFbx.so or libfalcor2_adobe_usdFbx.dylib.
Relative runtime search paths resolve dependencies in that directory.
Use debug/lib and the Debug registry with the Debug Falcor2 runtime.

Then use falcor2.pxr.Usd.Stage.Open() or falcor2.UsdImporter().load_scene() with an
absolute FBX filename. Generic scene dispatch and automatic deployment are not
part of this experiment. Never load this plugin into an unrelated pxr runtime.

FBX is the only supported format feature. Shared image helpers use OpenImageIO
and ArResolver instead of Hio. SBSAR/Hio procedural image providers are not
supported. USD, its overlay, and the existing triplets are unchanged.
